        "original_id": "353185c6-91ef-5d82-8f7b-e7a79d785e47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Age of Chance, Vector, Steve Taylor & The Perfect Foil\n- Albums: One Thousand Years of Trouble\n- People: Jimmy Abegg, Steve Griffith, Charlie Peacock, Steve Taylor, Peter Furler, John Mark Painter\n- Places: Leeds, England, Sacramento, California\n- Companies: Virgin Records\n\nFacts:\n- Vector was a rock band formed in Sacramento, California, in the early 1980s by Jimmy Abegg, Steve Griffith, and Charlie Peacock.\n- Age of Chance were a British alternative rock-dance crossover band from Leeds, England, active from 1985 to 1991.\n- One Thousand Years of Trouble is the debut full-length album and second album overall by the English electronic rock band Age of Chance, and Virgin Records released it in 1987.\n- Steve Taylor & The Perfect Foil is an American alternative rock supergroup formed in 2010 by singer Steve Taylor with drummer Peter Furler, guitarist Jimmy Abegg, and bassist John Mark Painter.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
